rong>2.2161%</strong>; the spread is only about <strong>0.13 percentage points</strong>, suggesting discounting is broadly consistent.</li><li><strong>Inventory observations:</strong> inventory is healthy across all <strong>8 stores</strong> and <strong>424 products</strong>, with <strong>0 stockout rows</strong>. Total on-hand inventory is <strong>3,893,197 units</strong>; <em>Seattle</em> holds the most at <strong>946,964</strong>, followed by <em>Online</em> at <strong>898,779</strong> and <em>Bellevue</em> at <strong>714,421</strong>.</li></ul><p><em>Notable pattern:</em> high-revenue stores and high-inventory stores align at the top end, while lower-volume stores still maintain full assortment coverage, indicating the network is well stocked without visible stockout pressure.</p>",
